# port-patches.sh: glm/sampling-r7 @ 3c8b05d8bbb7 over glm/zig-engine-fixes-on-186 @ e027c49cd06d (commits 8d1796cc3ab1..3022ee57d656); regenerate with scripts/port-patches.sh, do not edit
glm_cuda: spill v2 for GLM: kept-state packing, the rank protocol, the compatibility fingerprint and the GLM tier behind TF_GLM_SPILL_V2=1 (port of GLM 0110)

The GLM family's half of spill v2, on the core store and the prompt cache's
Tier: every kept prompt state is written to each Spark's disk when it is kept
and read back beside decoding, also after a restart.

- cuda_spill_state: a kept state (one device buffer here, outside the pool)
  in shared 2,048-token blocks of the 11 DSA layers' latent rows and pooled
  index keys (6,204 bytes a token at TP=2), so a conversation's later turns
  write only their own blocks, and small per-point sections (the KDA states,
  conv windows, index rings and DFlash2's rings: ~103 MiB with the drafter);
  a release guard holds a state a queued write still reads.
- cuda_spill_wire and Flash Next's mirror: the ranks' messages ride the
  ordered record stream rank 1 already replays (keep, begin, progress,
  validate, settle, share/touch/forget, flush), asks every rank answers in
  one gather, every rank's counters at most once a second.
- cuda_spill_identity: the compatibility fingerprint (format, engine and
  recipe ids, the weights through their own headers, the drafter, the
  template, the shapes and the switches that change state), agreed by the
  ranks at start; it names each rank's store folder, so a point is only ever
  read by an engine that would have written the same bytes.
- cuda_spill_tier: rank 0's tier behind the prompt cache (lookup on the
  request's 64-token grid and chunk starts, write at keep, staging between
  rounds, restores with every rank's has, copies and validation, one verdict
  for all ranks, forget on damage, flush at a clean stop) and rank 1's side.
- TF_GLM_SPILL_V2=1 (with --spill-gib and --snapshot-dir): the pinned
  staging is taken before the KV pool is sized, the kept-state budget is
  agreed as the smallest over the ranks, every rank's store opens (or the
  start fails on all), its folders are given to the spill directory's owner,
  and the store's tier is set (v1 off).

Switches (both ranks, in the agreed settings text): TF_GLM_SPILL_V2 (0 = v1,
the rollback; 1 = v2, needs --spill-gib above 0 and --snapshot-dir),
TF_GLM_SPILL_QUOTA (0), TF_GLM_SPILL_TURNS (4), TF_GLM_SPILL_READ_BLOCKS (16),
TF_GLM_SPILL_STAGE_MIB (256), --spill-min-tokens (8192), --spill-min-free-gib
(50), --spill-flush-s; --spill-highwater is accepted and ignored under v2. The
identity: TF_GLM_ENGINE_ID, TF_GLM_RECIPE_PATCHES, TF_GLM_MODEL_REVISION,
TF_GLM_DFLASH2_REVISION (the recipe sets them). Refused: TP other than 2, MTP
drafts (the prompt cache is off with them), a kept-state budget of 0 on any
rank (with PROMPT_CACHE_GIB, a lower KV_POOL_GIB), a staging ring under two
blocks, TF_GLM_KV_SHARD=1 (until spill v2 with KV sharding). Off, nothing of
this runs: no staging, no word in the settings text, the same logs.

Tests (host): the packer over a host copier (whole states, tails, forks,
restores), the protocol's codecs, the fingerprint's fields and agreement, and
the tier over a host rig of two ranks (keep, stage, restore, damage on either
rank, restart, flush).

Measured on the pair (g2, round 2's image): spill v2 on, exact 39/39 identical
to the base engine; the ranks' identities agreed (the recipe's); staging 1,066
MiB taken before the pool, kept-state budget 5.1 GiB. spill_check main 20/22:
every seed equal to the baseline and committed on both ranks; evicted and
restored from disk, exact; a corrupt block or small section (rank 0), a
truncated one (rank 1) and a removed small section (rank 1) refused, replies
exact; three sizes; settled. Its dual-restore case failed (of two concurrent
restores one restored, the other prefilled from 0 although its point was on
disk, no spill eviction: points 36 a rank, 11.6 GB under a 16 GiB cap; the
cache tier's concurrent-restore rules fix it, not yet re-run on the pair) and
its cancel case was skipped. postrestart 4/4: points recovered (38/37), a
restore after the restart exact, a point missing on rank 1 refused and
forgotten on both, no temporaries left.

Credits: Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo); spill v2's block store
